Engine: a right click at a point, MSG_INJECT_RIGHT_CLICK 0x87 (open fix 61).

STATUS: APPLIED 30 September 2026 by work order 194 (Part A, "F12 view on
the combat map ... the right mouse button is not passed on") — orion2re
ab3f6892 on orionlayer-local (before: 96da4c4d), this file's diff byte for
byte (index lines included). Required by tools/version_check.py since work
order 194.

It was applied, from ~/orion2re on the orionlayer-local branch, with:

    patch -p1 < ~/orionlayerv3/doc/ext_inject_right_click.patch

and a rebuild. It comes back off with `git revert ab3f6892` or
`patch -R -p1`, and a rebuild.

WHAT IT IS FOR

    The battle map is one grid field (combat1.cpp:111). A RIGHT click on it
    turns the active ship to face the point: Get_Input_ returns the negated
    field and the loop reads `_cur_combat_x + _xpos / 2` (combat1.cpp:
    696-710). The wire had no right click at a point: INJECT_CLICK pushes the
    left button only, and CANCEL_FIELD right-clicks a field's CENTRE — the
    whole answer for a button, the wrong one for a grid. So the F12 view
    could not turn a ship. The change is INJECT_CLICK with the right button,
    under its own message type, so an engine without it drops the message
    (ProcessInput's `default: break`) instead of taking it as a left click
    (which would MOVE the ship).

    Written only in src/ext; nothing runs unless a client sends 0x87, so an
    engine without OrionLayer behaves exactly as before. One marker,
    `OrionLayer, open fix 61.`, on one line at each of the three changed
    places.

diff --git a/src/ext/ext_api.cpp b/src/ext/ext_api.cpp
index 248280bc..7c31af8f 100644
--- a/src/ext/ext_api.cpp
+++ b/src/ext/ext_api.cpp
@@ -1836,6 +1836,35 @@ static void ProcessInput() {
             g_hide_window = (cmd.param1 == 0);
             break;
 
+        case MSG_INJECT_RIGHT_CLICK:
+            // OrionLayer, open fix 61. INJECT_CLICK with the right button: a grid field reads the point (the battle map's turn-to-face, combat1.cpp:696-710).
+            {
+                // CANCEL_FIELD right-clicks a field's CENTRE, which is
+                // the whole answer for a button and the wrong one for a
+                // grid field: the game reads _xpos/_ypos from the point.
+                g_injected_mouse_pending = true;
+                float wx = 0.0f;
+                float wy = 0.0f;
+                Game_Point_To_Window_Point_((float)cmd.param1,
+                                            (float)cmd.param2,
+                                            &wx, &wy);
+                SDL_Event down{};
+                down.type = SDL_EVENT_MOUSE_BUTTON_DOWN;
+                down.button.button = SDL_BUTTON_RIGHT;
+                down.button.x = wx;
+                down.button.y = wy;
+                down.button.down = true;
+                SDL_PushEvent(&down);
+                SDL_Event up{};
+                up.type = SDL_EVENT_MOUSE_BUTTON_UP;
+                up.button.button = SDL_BUTTON_RIGHT;
+                up.button.x = wx;
+                up.button.y = wy;
+                up.button.down = false;
+                SDL_PushEvent(&up);
+            }
+            break;
+
         case MSG_CANCEL_FIELD:
             // Right-click on field (DOWN + UP)
             if (cmd.param1 >= 0 && cmd.param1 < fields::_fields_count) {
